@jamolpe88/dsh-desktop-chat README · Requirements：- **DSH Desktop** `>= 0.2.1-rc.3`, profile `desktop` (a plain web profile provides no native browser guest).
- Windows 11 (tested); macOS and Linux untested.
- No runtime dependencies; no separate Node installation required.

@jamolpe88/dsh-desktop-chat README · What is kept and what is not：DSH Desktop gives every browser view a **process-lifetime session partition** (a new random name on each
start). A plugin cannot change that, and there is no public API to read the partition's cookies. The session
is therefore preserved at the page level:

@jamolpe88/dsh-desktop-chat README · Diagnostics：`hasUserToken` is the signal that matters: if it is `false` after signing in, saving is not reaching the Host
and the session cannot survive. `last.save.diag` reports why a save was skipped (`not-ready`, `off-origin`,
`read-failed`…). The port changes on every DSH start; take it from the interface URL.
